## Summary — What's in each block

| # | System | Key entry points |
|---|--------|------------------|
| 1 | Core helpers | `AR2_carBase`, `AR2_carPick`, `AR2_carConfig`, `AR2_occupiedCar`, `AR2_ejectFromVehicle`, `AR2_carHealth` |
| 2 | Tuning mods | `AR2_carMods.apply()`, `AR2_sweep()`, `AR2_applyTo()` |
| 3 | Extra mods | `AR2_setBoatMode`, `AR2_setRemoveDrag`, `AR2_setFullSteer` |
| 4 | TP Dash | `AR2_startCarDash`, `AR2_stopCarDash` |
| 5 | Vehicle Noclip | `AR2_carNoclipStart`, `AR2_carNoclipSetEnabled`, `AR2_carNoclipStop` |
| 6 | Vehicle Noclip TP | `AR2_carNoclipTP.run/toPlayer/toPosition/stop` |
| 7 | Car Fly | `AR2_carFlyStart`, `AR2_carFlySetEnabled`, `AR2_carFlyStop` |
| 8 | Vehicle Equip | `AR2_setVehicleEquip` |

**External dependencies you'll still need to supply:**
- `AR2_localPosition()` — returns local player's world position
- `AR2_tpTargetRoot()` — returns root part of the selected TP target (used by `carNoclipTP.toPlayer`)
- `AR2_tp.toggleMap(on)` — only if you use the map-click wiring in block 10
- Metamethod helpers: `getrawmetatable`, `setreadonly`, `newcclosure`, `getgenv` (executor provided)
